<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-2205] clause HAVING doesn&apos;t work for count</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-2205</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The setup is similar to &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-2143&quot; title=&quot;inner join produce wrong result and is very slow&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-2143&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-2143&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Can be reproduced on a single node.&lt;br/&gt;
Query : &lt;br/&gt;
sharedRDD.sql(&quot;select lang, count(lang) as cnt from gitrecord group by lang having cnt &amp;gt; 5&quot;).show&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The result set contains all elements like there is no HAVING clause. That&apos;s reproducible only for count field. Others works like a charm.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
